  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "18. Transports",
    "ruleNumber": "18.02",
    "summary": "From battle round 1 on, a unit of yours can embark in a friendly **TRANSPORT** right after it ends a **normal**, **advance** or **fall-back move**, provided all of these hold:\n\n- Every model in the unit is no more than 3″ from the **TRANSPORT**.\n- The unit was not placed onto the battlefield this turn.\n- The **TRANSPORT**'s datasheet lists the unit as **eligible to embark**.\n- The **TRANSPORT** has enough **[transport capacity](vsdata:core-rule/transport-capacity)** left for the whole unit.\n\nThe active player then removes the unit from the battlefield; it is now embarked.",
